        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333872/comment/12381462",
          "id": "12381462",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ajmas%40bigfoot.com",
            "name": "ajmas@bigfoot.com",
            "key": "ajmas@bigfoot.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Andre John Mas",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Is this really an issue considering WordPad will open it without any problems.\nSecond, any adjustment to the textfile format will break the presentation on\nother platforms. Lastly, IMO, Notepad is a poor excuse for a text editor. I\nwould suggest using TextPad or UltradEdit as better alternatives.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ajmas%40bigfoot.com",
            "name": "ajmas@bigfoot.com",
            "key": "ajmas@bigfoot.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Andre John Mas",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2004-01-29T04:36:02.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-01-29T04:36:02.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333872/comment/12381463",
          "id": "12381463",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Hi Gary,\n\nI have to agree Andre here.  The files have EOLs, it's just that Notepad doesn't\nlike them.  The releases are built on linux and as such use the standard linux\nEOL when they are checked out of CVS.  \n\nIf you know of a simple, automated solution to modify EOLs for the .zip archives\nin Maven, I will gladly accept it.  If not, I do not think this is something\nthat will be changed.\n\nMike",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2004-01-29T05:19:29.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-01-29T05:19:29.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333872/comment/12381464",
          "id": "12381464",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=ggregory%40seagullsw.com",
            "name": "ggregory@seagullsw.com",
            "key": "ggregory@seagullsw.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10453",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10453",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10453",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10453"
            },
            "displayName": "ggregory@seagullsw.com",
            "active": false,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I think I've seen other projects to a LICENSE and README file (no extension)\nwith *NIX EOL and *.txt files with Win EOL. Ant could copy one to the other fix\nthe EOLs. Notepad is the default *.txt editor and sure loads *fast*. Not a\ncritical issue but makes folks feel better when file look normal on their OSs...",
